WEBVTT

00:00:00.116 --> 00:00:05.420
This video shows how to preview and download a student's report card on a phone.

00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:12.867
Tap the menu button at the top left, open Academics, and then choose Report Cards.

00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:18.209
Choose the class. Then tap the Student box and pick a student, here Sara Khan. The arrows beside the box move to the previous or the next student.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:41.686
The Session box shows the academic year, and the Exams box shows which exam the card is for. The newest ticked exam decides the result, so we tick Mid-Term 2026 and untick Weekly Quiz.

00:00:52.131 --> 00:01:09.459
Scroll down to read the report card: the student details, the marks for each subject, and the total and percentage. Below them are the position in the class and the date of issue. A Draft note says the results have not been announced yet, and only staff can see this preview.

00:01:16.286 --> 00:01:20.438
Tap Download PDF to save a printable report card.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.848
The report card is ready to print.
